diff --git a/docs/control-protocol.md b/docs/control-protocol.md
index 868e4bc..ac68704 100644
--- a/docs/control-protocol.md
+++ b/docs/control-protocol.md
@@ -35,6 +35,14 @@ The transport is `apps/photocraft/src/control_server.rs`, and the handlers are i
 - `engine.execute {command, params}`: run any engine or UI command by id. Engine commands run directly with their default params and never open a dialog. Use `ui.menu.invoke` for menu-click behaviour, which opens a command's dialog when no params are given. `params` must be a JSON object (omit it or pass `null` for none); an array, string, number or boolean is an error naming the command, in every transport (control channel, `serve`, MCP and the CLI)
 - `engine.commands`: list commands with enablement
 - `ui.inspect`: full UI state (tool, panels, views, dialogs, windows, window size). The menu tree is not included; use `ui.menu.list`. `view` holds the View/Window/Type preferences: `screen_mode`, `extras`, `show` and `snap_to` flags, `flip_horizontal`, `arrange` (Window › Arrange layout), pixel aspect, font preview size, language options. `perf.timings.gpuInfo` holds the graphics adapter, backend, driver, the backend chosen at launch and why, the canvas renderer (`gpu`/`cpu`) and, after a device loss, `lost` (`help.systemInfo` returns the same as `info`)
+- Launch flag `--raw-workspace` (Camera Raw first): Camera Raw opens by itself on each document and is drawn inside the main window (as the web build does) instead of in a window of its own; OK or Cancel leaves the ordinary editor on the same, still-open document, and it is not reopened for that document. Works with `--hosted`. A document Camera Raw cannot open on (no pixels it can work on) is left to the full editor with the reason in the status bar. See `crates/ui-egui/src/raw_workspace.rs`.
+- `ui.cameraRaw {open?, commit?, cancel?}` (Camera Raw workspace): no flags returns `{open, changed, applied, workspace}`; `open` opens Camera Raw on the active document; `commit` applies it the way a photo switch does (changed settings as one history step, an untouched dialog just closes, so browsing past a photo never edits or re-saves it); `cancel` closes it without applying. Only one flag at a time. In the workspace, `app.open` and `app.stash` commit an open dialog first, so a host that forgets cannot lose adjustments.
+- `app.open {path, replace?, cameraRaw?: {recipe?, recipePath?, displayPath?, continueFrom?}}` in the Camera Raw workspace: a raw is developed from its sensor data with the fast Malvar-He-Cutler demosaic (~1 s on 45 MP, against ~3 s for the default AHD) and opens in Camera Raw (the open-time dialog, `target: openRaw`) instead of as a smart object. `recipe` is the photo's stored Camera Raw settings (`{version: 1, cameraRaw: {...non-default settings}}`) the dialog starts from; `recipePath` (`.json`) and `displayPath` (`.jpg`) are write-root paths where the recipe and a screen-sized render of it are kept whenever the dialog is left with changes; `continueFrom` (a `.pcraft` path) makes **Open** continue that saved document instead of developing a new one. The reply carries `cameraRaw: {dialog: true|false}`: `false` means the file could not be developed from sensor data (an embedded-preview fallback opened instead) and the host should take its own route for it. Rejected unless the workspace is on and `rawSmartObject` is not set.
+- `app.prefetch {path, signature}` (Camera Raw workspace): develop the raw at `path` for Camera Raw in the background (one low-priority thread, one slot: a 45 MP photo is ~450 MB, and a newer request replaces an older one). `signature` is the file's `"<bytes>:<mtime_ns>"` as the host saw it; a later `app.open {cameraRaw: {signature}}` for the same path and signature then only adds the prepared document (the open job took 16 ms against ~3.4 s), and anything else is read afresh. Replies at once `{queued}`.
+- `app.open`'s `cameraRaw` also takes `signature` (see `app.prefetch`).
+- `ui.cameraRaw` also takes `done`: leave the photo. A raw's dialog keeps its settings as the recipe (written to `recipePath`, render to `displayPath`) and develops or applies nothing; any other dialog applies as `commit` does. `commit` on a raw's dialog is **Open**: develop with the settings, or continue `continueFrom`. The reply carries `target` (`openRaw`, `newFilter`, `smartFilter`), `recipe` and the leaving result.
+- Rendering notes for hosts: while the Camera Raw workspace has the window (its dialog is open or queued, or a raw that is only being browsed is the active document) the editor does not draw the document's own canvas. A full refresh of a document above 16 MP on a GPU that is not discrete is composited by the banded CPU path (45 MP: 2.6 s against 12-23 s through the wgpu compositor on an Intel UHD 620); `PHOTOCRAFT_FULL_REFRESH=gpu|cpu` overrides it.
+- `ui.viewport`: where the image is drawn, in physical window pixels, without `ui.inspect`'s cost: `window {width, height, pixelsPerPoint}`, `canvas {x, y, width, height}` and `cameraRaw` (`null`, or `{open: true, view, preview}`: `view` is the rectangle the Camera Raw dialog shows its photo in, `preview` the photo's own rectangle inside it, each `null` until the dialog has been laid out). A host that paints a cached picture over the embedded window uses it to cover only the image and leave the panels visible.
