-- `app.stash {path, preview, wait?}`: capture the active document's COW snapshot and save its layered project plus rendered preview on a worker without locking editing. With `wait: false`, returns `{job, pending: true}`; use `jobs.list` to observe success or failure. `app.open` can restore recent, pending or failed snapshots directly from memory. Failed snapshots remain available for retry; three successfully saved photos stay cached for fast return navigation. The desktop control path also reads and decodes ordinary `app.open` requests on a worker and replies once the document is ready. Neither path invokes ambient script events or color-policy file I/O.
+- `app.stash {path, preview, display?, wait?}`: capture the active document's COW snapshot and save its layered project plus rendered preview on a worker without locking editing. With `wait: false`, returns `{job, pending: true}`; use `jobs.list` to observe success or failure. `app.open` can restore recent, pending or failed snapshots directly from memory. Failed snapshots remain available for retry; three successfully saved photos stay cached for fast return navigation. The desktop control path also reads and decodes ordinary `app.open` requests on a worker and replies once the document is ready. Neither path invokes ambient script events or color-policy file I/O. With `display` (a `.jpg` under the write root), the stash also writes a screen-sized (2560 px long side) untagged-sRGB JPEG of the same snapshot, built from the compositor's reduced render beside the project encode and written as soon as it is ready, so a host can show an edited photo from a cached render while browsing. A failure to write it adds a warning and never fails the save.
 
